<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><h1>Privacy policy</h1><p>How candidate information is handled.</p></div></section><section class="container section prose"><div class="alert alert-warning"><strong>LEGAL REVIEW REQUIRED:</strong> The sections marked [LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED] must be completed for the jurisdictions in which GEST operates before accepting real candidates.</div><h2>1. Data controller and contact</h2><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: full controller name, registration details, address, DPO/privacy contact and governing law.]</p><h2>2. Information collected</h2><p>GEST processes your identity information, contact details, date of birth, nationality, first language, ID document number and encrypted document copies (PDF or image), a centre-captured identity photograph, bookings, payment status, attendance records and test results. We record your express consent when registering and completing your profile.</p><h2>3. Purposes and lawful bases</h2><p>Information is used to register candidates, verify identity at test centres, conduct test administration, issue and validate results and detect fraud.</p><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: jurisdiction-specific lawful bases, consent rights and contractual/legitimate-interest balancing.]</p><h2>4. Access and disclosures</h2><p>Your authorised test centre may download identity documents for booked candidates in its own sessions, and access relevant candidate identity, attendance and result details. GEST headquarters may access records for administration and approval. Certificate holders who share their form number and security code enable receiving organisations to verify relevant result details.</p><h2>5. Retention</h2><p>GEST maintains an administrative retention setting and handles deletion requests subject to applicable legal obligations. A controlled, dry-run-first retention cleanup script is provided but not automatically scheduled; GEST must establish its legally approved erasure and archival process before production operation.</p><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: actual retention schedule, archival requirements and international transfer details.]</p><h2>6. Your rights</h2><p>Logged-in candidates can download their stored personal information as JSON and their uploaded identity document separately and submit an account deletion request through their dashboard.</p><p>[LEGAL TEXT REQUIRED: access/rectification/objection/complaint rights, regulator details and response timelines.]</p><h2>7. Security and cookies</h2><p>GEST uses password hashing, AES-256-GCM encryption of uploaded identity documents at rest, restricted staff access, HTTPS-only secure cookies in production, security token validation and audit logging. Uploaded documents are not served from public folders. Real-world PDF antivirus scanning and an external security assessment are still required before production. A necessary session cookie supports sign-in and form security.</p></section>
